description:
RISK-6 (design/11-risk-register.md): `ibm_db`'s bundled clidriver auto-download happens at install time; it fails silently rather than loudly on restricted/air-gapped networks, needs manual `IBM_DB_WIN_DLL_DIR` setup on Windows (already referenced in `db/connection.py`, confirmed by VER-1's own verification comment), and macOS ARM64 needs a pinned clidriver version. Lower priority than FLEX-1..3 — this is an enterprise-adoption smoothness issue, not a correctness or scaling risk.

Scope:
(a) an install-time or first-connection check that fails loudly with a clear remediation message instead of silently, in each of the 3 scenarios;
(b) a dedicated "Installation troubleshooting" section in README.md covering air-gapped, Windows, and ARM64 explicitly;
(c) evaluate whether a pre-flight doctor-style command (in the spirit of `scripts/check_connection.py`) could catch driver issues before a user hits a cryptic runtime error, and implement it if the evaluation supports it.

Acceptance: each of the 3 failure scenarios produces an actionable error message, not a silent failure or generic traceback; README has the new troubleshooting section; default happy-path install behavior is unchanged.
